A||N||22||fropuff||Where to go for 3.4???||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||03-20-2001||05:22 PM||||Hey there.  I'm thinking of getting a 3.4L push rod engine for the GT.  I don't want to get the DOHC, as everyone says it's harder.  I was wondering if anyone knows were I can find a cheap, low-mileage (&lt;50K) 3.4L, other than a salvage yard.  The ones around here don't have any Camaros or Firebirds.  I was also wondering if anyone knows the cost of getting it installed professionally, like Ed Parks, Chris West, etc.  Some of the sites don't have prices.  I want to turbo charge the 3.4 if I get one, but all I want to know is where to get an engine, as well as where to get it installed for the lowest cost.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||03-20-2001||05:37 PM||||Oh, and before anyone goes and gets all pissy,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I did run a SEARCH many times.  I just couldn't find what I was looking for.  If anyone has a specific place to look, short of the SEARCH option, go ahead and post it.  I won't get mad at you for getting pissy.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000002||tgowens||03-20-2001||05:45 PM||||call George at the Fiero Shop at 866-534-8486 (toll free) - we have installed many 3.4's and can answer any of your questions...........||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||03-20-2001||06:58 PM||||Well, I found that the ACE kit for the 3.4L is $1800 US.  A little steep for me, considering that not much needs to be modified.  Any other help is greatly appreciated.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||03-20-2001||08:52 PM||||Well:<BR>-I found a site where there was a kit for $4200, engine included.<BR>-I found a site where a guy did a complete kit for $2200, engine was $800.  Not for sale, but he did it.  It's a 3.4 TDC.  <A HREF="http://www.fieros.org/osg/mod.3400-TDC-V6.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieros.org/osg/mod.3400-TDC-V6.html</A> <BR>-I found a 3.4 on eBay for $975.  I wouldn't get this one; not much crap to come with it.  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&Item=570477565" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&Item=570477565</A> <P>I don't know if I still want a 3.4 mod; I don't want to spend much money; &lt;$2500.  Any help appreciated.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Uaana||03-20-2001||08:55 PM||||You might want to get ahold of elfiero<BR>He's with MFF and I'm pretty sure he does engine swaps. Nice guy met him at the one event I made it to last year.<BR>His email is: fiero@go.com ||||reg||1
Z||000006||jlruiz67||03-20-2001||09:28 PM||||Here is a link with a price guide, they only provide a 30 day warranty, as far as I know .<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||03-20-2001||10:13 PM||||Alright, I went to the site that jlruiz gave me; $350-450 for a complete block with a fuel injection unit.  That's all; no accessories.  What accessories do I need?  I saw a short list on one site, but not all the required components.  I'm going to e-mail elfiero and ask him if he would do it for me; thanks a lot guys.  Your help is appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||03-20-2001||10:52 PM||||Click the TN Fiero link below and call Keith at Grooms and see what he can get you one of their new engines for... Great thing about them is that they are zero miles and come with an 18 month/unlimited mileage warranty. That's worth paying a little more than you would for a junyard engine. There is an 800 number there for any of you that don't live in Nashville.. and they do deliver!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||03-20-2001||10:57 PM||||Thanks a lot.  The only reason that I want a salvage yard engine is that it is already broken in, so I don't have to take the time to do all that crap.  I'll give the guy a call.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||03-20-2001||11:06 PM||||Since we've got the minn-eh-soo-tah people in here I'm gonna shoot a few questions..<P>Anybody around here done the 3.4 TDC swap, or know where I can get a good 3.4 TDC?  I really want to do this swap.  Maybe over next winter... hmmmm...<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tina||03-20-2001||11:12 PM||||Don't want to discourage you,<BR>just remember.<BR>"You can't get a steak for the price of a hamburger"<P>E-mail off list for the # of my mechanic.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||fropuff||03-21-2001||09:39 AM||||Thanks guys (and girls).  Standard, the reason I want to do the "regular" 3.4 and not the DOHC is that:<P>1) It's relatively cheaper to buy an engine<BR>2) It's a lot easier to install; therefore, cheaper to have it installed<BR>3) Less has to be modified on the engine<BR>4) The normal 3.4 pushrod engine can be dressed up identical to the stock 2.8<BR>5) I want to turbo charge.<P>I would really like the 3.4 DOHC, but I've heard that it is a lot easier to do the normal one.  I also think that dressing it up just like the 2.8 would be cool.  And, I do want to turbo charge, like Dennis LaGrua did on his 87 GT.  I want to do the 3.4 this summer, save a little, then manufacture a turbo system for it next summer.<P>Thanks again.<P>PS: Here's a site:  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A> <P>Sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||03-21-2001||01:57 PM||||Yeah, I completly understand that.  It is quite possible to turbo the TDC, though.  From what I hear, Chris West's turbo 3.4 TDC is running 350+ horsepower.  I've just decided that instead of going to a 3.4 pushrod, I'll just give my 2.8 a decent rebuild and go to 3.4 TDC when I have the money.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Uaana||03-21-2001||09:17 PM||||Since we have some MN people in here.<BR>Has anyone taken a look at this car?<BR>The number looks like a NW suburb #<BR>And for 2 grand wouldnt be that bad if it's not rusted out.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.carsoup.com/UsedVehicles/detail.asp?uvid=365746&startRow=1&FirstRec=0&OrderBy=&Sort=&searchid=3875307" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carsoup.com/UsedVehicles/detail.asp?uvid=365746&startRow=1&FirstRec=0&OrderBy=&Sort=&searchid=3875307</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||jch82||03-22-2001||07:05 PM||||Email Ken (MooCow), he is on the forum as well. His address is MooCow888@aol.com  His 87GT had a 3.4 and a 4:10 tranny installed by Ed Park's. We went down there to pick it up back in January. His fiero is very very fast now!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||03-22-2001||07:28 PM||||Your probably looking for something a little cheaper, but you may want to look into getting a 3.4L crate engine from GM too.  I am leaning towards going this route when my 2.8 finally gives in.  I like the idea of getting a new engine instead of a junkyard motor.  Just my personal preferance of course, 'cuz I know many people have found great engines in the yards!||||reg||1
Z||000017||fropuff||03-23-2001||04:23 PM||||Well, elfiero got back to me, and I think I'm going to go with the 3.4 pushrod.  There is a $2000 in installation alone (between the 3.4 pushrod and the 3.4 TDC/DOHC), so there'll be around a $3000 difference between engine cost and installation.  With that $3000, I can make me a nice turbo setup!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  He said that he's free in the summer (June or July), so now all I need is some money. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fropuff||03-23-2001||04:23 PM||||Well, elfiero got back to me, and I think I'm going to go with the 3.4 pushrod.  There is a $2000 in installation alone (between the 3.4 pushrod and the 3.4 TDC/DOHC), so there'll be around a $3000 difference between engine cost and installation.  With that $3000, I can make me a nice turbo setup!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  He said that he's free in the summer (June or July), so now all I need is some money. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000019||fropuff||03-23-2001||04:25 PM||||Well, elfiero got back to me, and I think I'm going to go with the 3.4 pushrod.  There is a $2000 in installation alone (between the 3.4 pushrod and the 3.4 TDC/DOHC), so there'll be around a $3000 difference between engine cost and installation.  With that $3000, I can make me a nice turbo setup!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  He said that he's free in the summer (June or July), so now all I need is some money. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000020||fropuff||03-26-2001||01:09 AM||||Well, after a weekend of thinking about it, I changed my mind again.  I figured that I'm going to make around $1200 from now to June.  Not enough to even have a 3.4L installed, let alone buy the engine itself.  I'm going to get a second job this summer, and I figured that I will make a total of $5000.  Okay, a turbo setup from Design One costs $3000, with everything down to the last screw.  I thought of doing my own setup for cheaper, but I am not an expert by far.  I will get the first "edition" of the turbo, then install it this fall/winter, or have elfiero install it for me, if he will do that.  I will have $2000 to pay off my dad, insurance, etc.  Good deal, I think.  Let me know what you think.  It's important.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000021||fropuff||03-26-2001||05:22 PM||||By the way, the $3000 figure I came up with is just the engine and installation; no turbo.  So, for that $3000, I can get 160 HP and 210 lb/ft of torque.  Now, I can spend the same and reach 200+ HP w/o any mods as of yet.  I want to build my own turbo setup, but I am no expert.  That $3000 is a little steep for me, but I guess I'll have to live with it.  If my 2.8 ever goes, I might get either a 3.1 or a 3.4L.  Does anyone know if the Design One turbo setup will fit on larger engines?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000022||fropuff||03-27-2001||05:40 PM||||Well, I've changed my mind...again!  I've decided that I don't want to go with a turbo kit, but rather build a turbo setup my own, with a lot of help from you guys!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I thought about it, and if I can build one for $1500, I would still have $3500 left over from the summer.  I can pay my dad and insurance off, and still have some left over for a winter car.  I'm going to do a little more research on this; I'm thinking of going the way of Dennis LaGrua.  Let me know what you think.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
